{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794462711,"nonce":"DepF+agunskKTTWnE0dDOa4bI6c=","title":"x","message":"After the build/push split (#182), the build library's `image` Step holds no registry credential, so BuildKit can't pull a private base image (`FROM \u003cprivate ECR/GHCR\u003e`). The pilot's base images may be in private ECR.\n\nWanted: a read-only pull credential that can reach the build Step without bringing back a push credential.\n- Must be a separate credential from the push one (not the same REGISTRY_AUTH or IRSA push role). A RUN that gets past the capability rule (6f54105) then reads at most pull access.\n- Shapes to choose from:\n  (a) a second core primitive, e.g. `registry_auth: pull`, backed by its own secret name (REGISTRY_PULL_AUTH) and a grant of its own;\n  (b) ECR only: the build Step's own profile with a pull-only IRSA role plus a login init container, routed with the per-Step `placement_profiles` map; docs-only, no core change;\n  (c) the forge's registry token with read-only scope (GHCR `read:packages`).\n- Fork PRs: a pull credential for a fork's build is still a leak of read access to private images. Decide whether forks get it.\n- Docs: the ECR page (#183 rewrite) shows (b) if it's chosen.\n\nRelated: 6f54105, dfa1b5f, 8c62098, ace8135.","files":null}]}